---
layout: article
title: Limits and retention
description: Appwrite Analytics plan limits for events, properties, and data retention, and the size limits for events, properties, and metric queries.
---

This page lists how many events Appwrite Analytics accepts on each plan, how long the data stays readable, and the size limits that apply to every event and request.

# Plan limits {% #plans %}

| | Free | Start | Pro | Enterprise |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Events | 50K per month per organization | 50K per month per project | 100K per month per project | Custom |
| Additional events | Not available | $3 per 100K events | $3 per 100K events | Custom |
| Properties | 1 per project | Unlimited | Unlimited | Unlimited |
| Data retention | 30 days | 90 days | 90 days | Custom |

On the Free plan, the events limit covers every property in the organization. On Start and Pro, each project has its own limit, which covers every property in that project. The limit counts every accepted event, including automatic events such as `scroll_depth` and `engagement_time`. Events from a datacenter network or a Firebase Test Lab device don't count, even when they come from a named bot such as GPTBot. Events your server sends with an API key always count. See [Bots and AI traffic](/docs/products/analytics/bots#billing).

For the rest of each plan, see [Pricing](/pricing).

# At the limit {% #at-the-limit %}

- **Events**: on the Free plan, once the organization reaches its monthly events limit, Appwrite rejects new events with a `402` `limit_analytics_events_exceeded` error until the next billing cycle. On Start and Pro, events past a project's limit are billed as additional events. The dashboard and `listMetrics` keep working past the events limit. If the organization reaches its [budget cap](/docs/advanced/billing/payments#budget-cap), Appwrite rejects new events with a `402` `budget_limit_exceeded` error.
- **Properties**: on the Free plan, once a project has its one property, **Create property** is unavailable, and the API rejects new properties with a `402` `analytics_property_limit_exceeded` error.
- **Rate limit**: Appwrite accepts up to 1,000 events a minute from one IP address for each property. Server-side events sent with an `analytics.write` key share a limit of 10,000 a minute for each property. Events past the limit are dropped, and the response has a `Retry-After` header with the seconds to wait.

# Retention {% #retention %}

Your plan's retention period sets how far back the dashboard and `listMetrics` can read. When the selected range reaches past it, such as **Last 12 months** on the Free plan, the range starts at the oldest readable date.

Appwrite stores events for 180 days on every plan, then deletes them. No plan's retention period, including a custom Enterprise one, reaches further back than those 180 days.

# Event limits {% #event-limits %}

- `name`: 1 to 64 characters.
- `url`: required, with a scheme such as `https://`.
- `domain`: up to 255 characters.
- `referrer`: up to 2,048 characters.
- `scrollDepth`: `0` to `100`.
- `engagementTime`: `0` to `4294967295` seconds.
- `sessionHash`: up to 128 characters.
- `props`: up to 32 items, so 16 key and value pairs, each up to 255 characters.
- `userId`: up to 64 characters.
- `ip`: up to 45 characters.
- `userAgent`: up to 2,048 characters.
- `interactive`: `true` or `false`.

An event over any limit is rejected with a `400` `general_argument_invalid` error.

# Property limits {% #property-limits %}

- **Property ID**: up to 36 characters. Letters, numbers, periods, hyphens, and underscores, not starting with a special character.
- **Name**: up to 128 characters.
- **Domain**: up to 255 characters.
- **Allowed origins**: up to 64 origins, each up to 255 characters.

# Metric query limits {% #query-limits %}

- `queries`: up to 10 filters.
- `dimensions`: one dimension per request.
- `limit`: 1 to 500 rows, 100 by default.

On the dashboard, the hourly **1h** interval is available for date ranges of 31 days or less.
